Z||000000||b lo 0||08-01-2000||12:31 PM||||I was going through my '85 GT's driver's door panel last night to fix the PDL actator and take off the hinges to change the bushings in the lower hinge pin (btw, does anyone know how to do that without taking the outer skin off?  Or a method of changing the bushings without taking the door off?) and noticed there are no mounting points for the manual mirror joystick.  There are these little plates of metal attached to the joystick, but they have no holes in them and look like they were cut with a hacksaw.  How does the joystick thing mount?  Neither of my service manuals say anything about them.  I ask because the joystick is loose and thus, the interior panel is detached-looking at the top.  Please help me!!<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">    <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||DaveL||08-01-2000||03:34 PM||||The business end of the cable sticks into the little plastic holder on the top of the door panel, and is tightened with a small allen wench. Make that a wrench...||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||08-02-2000||06:56 AM||||If you are taking about how it mounts under the door panel, there is supposed to be a couple little bolts that hold that plate on. Yours may not be original.||||reg||1
